index febd4f0..c0215cd 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,11 +3,45 @@
 Terraform for the reports bucket and the key the nightly export job uploads with. The job reads
 the key from `terraform output`.
 
-## Usage
+State is stored in S3 (versioned, KMS-encrypted, public access blocked, TLS-only, native S3
+lockfile locking so no DynamoDB table is needed). Requires Terraform >= 1.10.
+
+## One-time bootstrap (one person, once)
+
+`bootstrap/` creates the state bucket. Its own state is local (it can't live in a bucket that
+doesn't exist yet); it holds no secrets and can be re-imported if lost.
 
 ```sh
+cd bootstrap
 terraform init
+terraform apply          # bucket defaults to tfstate-<account id>-<region>
+terraform output -raw bucket
+```
+
+Optionally keep `bootstrap/terraform.tfstate` somewhere safe. The bucket has `prevent_destroy`.
+
+## Everyday workflow (everyone)
+
+Use AWS credentials with `s3:ListBucket` on the bucket and `s3:GetObject`/`PutObject`/`DeleteObject`
+on `reports/*` (the lockfile is `reports/terraform.tfstate.tflock`) plus KMS use of the S3 key.
+
+```sh
+terraform init -backend-config="bucket=<bucket from bootstrap output>"
+terraform plan
 terraform apply
 ```
 
-State is kept locally in `terraform.tfstate`, so only the person who last ran `apply` has it.
+## Migrating the existing local state (once, by whoever holds `terraform.tfstate`)
+
+```sh
+terraform init -migrate-state -backend-config="bucket=<bucket>"
+```
+
+Answer `yes` to copy the state, confirm with `terraform plan` (expect no changes), then delete the
+local `terraform.tfstate*` files. Do this before anyone else runs `apply`.
+
+## Notes
+
+- The state contains the IAM access key secret (`aws_iam_access_key.uploader`), so restrict bucket
+  access to people who may read that secret.
+- Never commit state files; `.gitignore` excludes them.
